  "interpretation": "The positive R_avail slope survives simultaneous stage, model, publication-year, input-length, and target-length adjustment. It also survives a stronger within-paper specification that absorbs every stable item attribute; stage interactions localize the positive association to S1 and S3 rather than the near-floor S0 stage.",
  "limitations": [
    "This is an associational sensitivity analysis, not a causal effect of recoverability on model score.",
    "Publication year is a coarse temporal proxy and does not establish model-specific training exposure or absence of contamination.",
    "The panel has budget-driven, unbalanced model coverage; model fixed effects and item-cluster resampling mitigate but do not remove every selection concern.",
    "Prediction length may be downstream of model behavior, so the generation-length-adjusted model is a conservative secondary specification.",
    "The primary exposure and outcome are lexical-family measures; scorer-disjoint and reverse-family analyses remain separate authorities.",
    "Item fixed effects remove stable paper-level heterogeneity but not unmeasured stage-varying confounding; the within-paper estimates remain associational.",
    "The stage-interaction model is a secondary heterogeneity analysis and the S0 slope is imprecise because recoverability is near its floor."
  ],
